1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,593
Titrations are named after the reaction they use.

2
00:00:03,593 --> 00:00:07,057
Acid base titrations use neutralisation.

3
00:00:07,057 --> 00:00:10,481
Redox titrations use electron transfer.

4
00:00:10,481 --> 00:00:17,161
Precipitation titrations, like silver nitrate against chloride, form an insoluble salt.

5
00:00:17,161 --> 00:00:21,341
Complexometric titrations use E D T A.

6
00:00:21,341 --> 00:00:28,606
And iodometric titrations use iodine and thiosulphate, with starch as the indicator.

7
00:00:28,606 --> 00:00:31,054
Our syllabus focuses on the first two.

